IMPORT prelude

-- Online Criminal Harms Act 2023 (Singapore) -- when a designated officer may direct that online material, locations, accounts or
-- apps be taken down or blocked (ss 2, 6, 7, First Schedule), who may challenge a direction and when (ss 15-18, 42, 43), the
-- offence of not complying, its defences and its maximum penalties (ss 50, 54), and the police power to demand information
-- about online activity (s 48).
--
-- Edition: informal consolidation, "version in force from 15/9/2026", as deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/OCHA2023.txt (retrieved 2026-10-05). The latest amendment annotated in the deposit is item 19A of
-- the First Schedule, "[Act 10 of 2025 wef 15/09/2026]"; S 559/2026 (wef 17/08/2026) and S 257/2026 (wef 01/05/2026) are also shown.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Chosen for its everyday-life relevance (Tier 1 of the remaining Acts): it is the law under which a post, a chat
-- group, a social-media account or an app that an ordinary person uses or runs can be ordered down because it is suspected of
-- furthering a crime, above all a scam. SCOPED to the Part 2 directions (the ones that reach individuals), their challenge, the
-- offence of non-compliance, and s 48. Not encoded: Part 4 (designated online services, codes of practice, rectification notices,
-- implementation directives) and the Part 5 appeals to the Minister; Part 6 orders (ss 28-37) beyond a mention; the composition and
-- procedure of Reviewing Tribunals beyond ss 42 and 43; service of notices (ss 45, 46); s 47; ss 51-53 penalties (s 53 is noted);
-- arrestability (s 55); immunity (s 57); and most of the First Schedule (only five offences are tested against it).
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the conventions of the example rows (the writing-l4-rules skill was not
-- available in this session). No pipeline, no coverage table, no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Online Criminal Harms Act 2023 -- Part 2 directions`

§§ `2 and First Schedule -- specified offences and scam offences`

-- First Schedule Part 1 (specified offences) lists 45 items, among them item 6 "Offences under the Computer Misuse Act 1993",
-- item 29 "Offences under the Penal Code 1871 (except Chapters 5, 5A and 23)", item 32 "Offences under Part 2 of the Protection from
-- Harassment Act 2014" and item 36 "Offence under section 116 of the Road Traffic Act 1961". It does NOT list the Securities and
-- Futures Act.
-- First Schedule Part 2 (scam or malicious cyber activity offences): item 1 the Computer Misuse Act 1993; item 2 "Chapters 12 and 18
-- and sections 170, 383 to 389, 405 to 409, 415 to 420A, 424A and 424B of the Penal Code 1871"; item 2A offences under SFA s 204
-- "for contravention of section 197, 199, 200, 201, 201A, 201B or 202" and under s 210 for contravention of s 207 or 209.
--
-- INFERENCE: that s 420 of the Penal Code is outside Chapters 5, 5A and 23 is not stated in the deposit; it is assumed here.
DECLARE Offence IS ONE OF
    `an offence under Penal Code s 420`
    `an offence under the Computer Misuse Act 1993`
    `an offence under SFA s 204 for contravening s 197`
    `an offence under Part 2 of the Protection from Harassment Act 2014`
    `an offence under Road Traffic Act 1961 s 67`

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a specified offence` IF
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `an offence under SFA s 204 for contravening s 197` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `an offence under Road Traffic Act 1961 s 67` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a scam or malicious cyber activity offence` IF
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `an offence under Penal Code s 420` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `an offence under the Computer Misuse Act 1993` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `an offence under SFA s 204 for contravening s 197` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `6(1) -- when a Part 2 direction may be given`

-- s 6(1): a designated officer may give a Part 2 direction if he or she "(a) reasonably suspects that a specified offence has been
-- committed and that any online activity is in furtherance of the commission of the offence; or (b) suspects or has reason to
-- believe that any online activity is preparatory to, or in furtherance of, the commission of a scam or malicious cyber activity
-- offence."
-- So for scams the bar is lower twice over: suspicion need not be reasonable, and the offence need not yet have been committed.
-- INFERENCE: an officer who reasonably suspects also "suspects" for limb (b).
DECLARE Suspicion IS ONE OF
    `no suspicion`
    `suspicion or reason to believe`
    `reasonable suspicion`

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence,
      `the officer's suspicion` IS A Suspicion,
      `the offence is suspected to have been committed` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the activity is suspected to further the offence` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the activity is suspected to be preparatory to the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a Part 2 direction may be given` IF
        (    `is a specified offence` `the offence`
         AND `the officer's suspicion` EQUALS `reasonable suspicion`
         AND `the offence is suspected to have been committed`
         AND `the activity is suspected to further the offence`)
    OR  (    `is a scam or malicious cyber activity offence` `the offence`
         AND (NOT `the officer's suspicion` EQUALS `no suspicion`)
         AND (`the activity is suspected to further the offence` OR `the activity is suspected to be preparatory to the offence`))

§§ `7 -- to whom each direction may be given`

-- s 7 table: 1 stop communication -- "A person who has control of the relevant material or the proprietor of the relevant location";
-- 2 disabling -- "The provider of an online service, excluding an internet access service or app distribution service"; 3 access
-- blocking -- "The provider of an internet access service"; 4 account restriction -- as for disabling; 5 app removal -- "The provider
-- of an app distribution service".
-- s 6(2): to any individual or entity, resident or not, in Singapore or not. s 13(3): "It is not necessary to give any person who
-- may be affected by a Part 2 direction a chance to be heard before the direction is given."
-- An ordinary user who posted something can be given only a stop communication direction.
DECLARE Direction IS ONE OF
    `stop communication direction`
    `disabling direction`
    `access blocking direction`
    `account restriction direction`
    `app removal direction`

DECLARE Recipient IS ONE OF
    `a person who controls the material`
    `the proprietor of the online location`
    `an online service provider (not internet access or app distribution)`
    `an internet access service provider`
    `an app distribution service provider`

GIVEN `the direction` IS A Direction, `the recipient` IS A Recipient
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the direction may be given to the recipient` IF
    CONSIDER `the direction`
    WHEN `stop communication direction` THEN
        CONSIDER `the recipient`
        WHEN `a person who controls the material` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `the proprietor of the online location` THEN TRUE
        OTHERWISE FALSE
    WHEN `disabling direction` THEN `the recipient` EQUALS `an online service provider (not internet access or app distribution)`
    WHEN `account restriction direction` THEN `the recipient` EQUALS `an online service provider (not internet access or app distribution)`
    WHEN `access blocking direction` THEN `the recipient` EQUALS `an internet access service provider`
    WHEN `app removal direction` THEN `the recipient` EQUALS `an app distribution service provider`

§§ `15 -- who may seek reconsideration or appeal`

-- s 15 table. The PDF columns are shifted in the deposit, so the appellants are matched to the rows BY ORDER: 1 stop communication --
-- the recipient; 2 disabling -- (a) the recipient, (b) the proprietor of the relevant location, (c) the originator of the relevant
-- material; 3 access blocking -- the same three; 4 account restriction -- (a) the recipient, (b) the proprietor of the relevant
-- account; 5 app removal -- (a) the recipient, (b) the owner of the relevant app.
-- s 2: "originator" means "the person who posted the relevant material, and excludes any other person who reposts identical copies".
DECLARE Appellant IS ONE OF
    `the recipient`
    `the location's proprietor`
    `the material's originator`
    `the account's proprietor`
    `the app's owner`
    `a person who reposted identical copies`

GIVEN `the direction` IS A Direction, `the challenger` IS AN Appellant
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the challenger may seek reconsideration or appeal` IF
        `the challenger` EQUALS `the recipient`
    OR  CONSIDER `the direction`
        WHEN `disabling direction` THEN `the challenger` EQUALS `the location's proprietor` OR `the challenger` EQUALS `the material's originator`
        WHEN `access blocking direction` THEN `the challenger` EQUALS `the location's proprietor` OR `the challenger` EQUALS `the material's originator`
        WHEN `account restriction direction` THEN `the challenger` EQUALS `the account's proprietor`
        WHEN `app removal direction` THEN `the challenger` EQUALS `the app's owner`
        OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `16, 17, 18 and 43(1) -- reconsideration, then the Reviewing Tribunal`

-- s 16(2)(b): an application for reconsideration must be made "not later than 30 days after being given the Part 2 direction";
-- (3) it "does not affect the operation of the Part 2 direction".
-- s 17(1): the designated officer must affirm, cancel or substitute. s 18(1): an appellant who receives notice "of the decision to
-- affirm or substitute" may, on payment of a prescribed fee, appeal to a Reviewing Tribunal; (2) the appeal does not suspend the
-- direction. s 43(1): the Tribunal "must not consider or determine" an appeal made more than 30 days after the notice of decision,
-- "Except where a Reviewing Tribunal ... is satisfied that it is equitable to do so". There is no appeal without reconsideration first.
GIVEN `days since the direction was given` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the reconsideration application is in time` IF
    `days since the direction was given` AT MOST 30

DECLARE Decision IS ONE OF
    `affirmed`
    `cancelled`
    `substituted`

GIVEN `the reconsideration decision` IS A Decision,
      `days since notice of the decision` IS A NUMBER,
      `the Tribunal finds it equitable` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Reviewing Tribunal may consider the appeal` IF
        (NOT `the reconsideration decision` EQUALS `cancelled`)
    AND (`days since notice of the decision` AT MOST 30 OR `the Tribunal finds it equitable`)

§§ `42(1) -- the only grounds on which the Tribunal may cancel a Part 2 direction`

-- s 42(1): a Reviewing Tribunal "may only cancel a Part 2 direction" on these grounds: "(a) the requirements of section 6(1) were not
-- satisfied; (b) the person that was given the direction was not a person to whom the direction may be given under section 7;
-- (c) it is not reasonably practicable to comply with the direction." s 41(3): it may affirm or cancel, nothing else; (5) final.
GIVEN `the direction` IS A Direction,
      `the recipient` IS A Recipient,
      `section 6(1) was satisfied` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `compliance is reasonably practicable` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Tribunal may cancel the direction` IF
        (NOT `section 6(1) was satisfied`)
    OR  (NOT `the direction may be given to the recipient` `the direction` `the recipient`)
    OR  (NOT `compliance is reasonably practicable`)

§§ `50 and 54 -- the offence of not complying, and its defences`

-- s 50(1)-(5): a person given a Part 2 direction who "without reasonable excuse, fails to comply with any requirement of the
-- direction" commits an offence, "whether in Singapore or outside Singapore".
-- s 54(1): "It is not a defence" that (a) a duty under written law, rule of law, contract or professional conduct prevents compliance,
-- or (b) "the person has applied for a reconsideration of, or has appealed against" the direction.
-- s 54(3): "(except in relation to a stop communication direction)" it is a defence if the accused proves, on a balance of
-- probabilities, that it was not reasonably practicable to do more than was done, or there was no better practicable means.
-- The two s 54(1) facts are parameters that the rule deliberately ignores.
GIVEN `the direction` IS A Direction,
      `complied` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `had a reasonable excuse` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `proved it did all that was reasonably practicable` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `has applied for reconsideration or appealed` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `a contract or duty of confidence forbids compliance` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `not complying is an offence` IF
        (NOT `complied`)
    AND (NOT `had a reasonable excuse`)
    AND (NOT (    (NOT `the direction` EQUALS `stop communication direction`)
              AND `proved it did all that was reasonably practicable`))

§§ `50(6)-(8) -- maximum penalties`

-- s 50(6) stop communication: individual "$20,000 or ... imprisonment for a term not exceeding 2 years or to both"; any other case
-- "$500,000".
-- s 50(7) disabling or account restriction: individual $20,000 or 12 months or both; any other case "$1 million"; and in either case
-- "a further fine not exceeding $100,000 for every day or part of a day during which the offence continues after conviction".
-- s 50(8) access blocking or app removal: "$20,000 for every day or part of a day" of non-compliance, "but not exceeding in total
-- $500,000" -- the same for individuals and others, and no imprisonment.
-- `days of non-compliance` counts every day or part of a day; the caller rounds part days up.
GIVEN `a` IS A NUMBER, `b` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the smaller of` MEANS
    IF `a` AT MOST `b` THEN `a` ELSE `b`

GIVEN `the direction` IS A Direction, `the offender is an individual` IS A BOOLEAN, `days of non-compliance` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the direction`
    WHEN `stop communication direction` THEN
        IF `the offender is an individual` THEN 20000 ELSE 500000
    WHEN `disabling direction` THEN
        IF `the offender is an individual` THEN 20000 ELSE 1000000
    WHEN `account restriction direction` THEN
        IF `the offender is an individual` THEN 20000 ELSE 1000000
    OTHERWISE `the smaller of` (20000 TIMES `days of non-compliance`) 500000

GIVEN `the direction` IS A Direction, `the offender is an individual` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum imprisonment in months` MEANS
    IF `the offender is an individual`
    THEN CONSIDER `the direction`
         WHEN `stop communication direction` THEN 24
         WHEN `disabling direction` THEN 12
         WHEN `account restriction direction` THEN 12
         OTHERWISE 0
    ELSE 0

GIVEN `the direction` IS A Direction
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the further fine per day after conviction` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the direction`
    WHEN `disabling direction` THEN 100000
    WHEN `account restriction direction` THEN 100000
    OTHERWISE 0

§§ `48 -- police demands for information about online activity`

-- s 48(1): where "a police officer of or above the rank of sergeant or an enforcement officer reasonably suspects that (a) a
-- specified offence has been committed; and (b) any online activity in furtherance of the offence has occurred", he or she may by
-- written notice require the provider of the online service or the proprietor of the online location to give information about the
-- activity, the account and its proprietor, and anything else to assist investigations. s 53(2): failing to comply without
-- reasonable excuse -- individual $5,000 or 6 months or both; otherwise $10,000. Scam offences that are not specified offences
-- (for example the SFA items) do not trigger s 48.
GIVEN `is a police officer of or above the rank of sergeant` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `is an enforcement officer` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the suspected offence` IS AN Offence,
      `reasonably suspects the offence was committed` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `reasonably suspects online activity furthered it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the officer may demand information` IF
        (`is a police officer of or above the rank of sergeant` OR `is an enforcement officer`)
    AND `is a specified offence` `the suspected offence`
    AND `reasonably suspects the offence was committed`
    AND `reasonably suspects online activity furthered it`
